<Layout title={seo.title} description={seo.description} keywords="portfolio tracker excel alternative, excel vs dedicated portfolio tracker, manual portfolio tracking problems, automated wealth tracker india, best portfolio tracker app india" schema={JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "5 Reasons You Should Stop Using Excel for Your Portfolio (2026)",
      "image": "https://arthavi.com/images/og-image.png",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Arthavi"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "Arthavi",
        "logo": {
          "@type": "ImageObject",
          "url": "https://arthavi.com/images/logo.png"
        }
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-02-16",
      "description": "Here are 5 reasons why modern investors in India are switching from Excel to automated privacy-first trackers."
    })}>

    

    <main class="container" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem);">
        <article class="prose fade-in" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
            <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">5 Reasons You Should Stop Using Excel for Your
                Portfolio (2026)</h1>

            <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
                We get it. Excel is comforting. You have total control, endless customization, and—best of all—nobody is
                spying on your data.
            </p>

            <p>For decades, the humble spreadsheet was the gold standard for tracking personal wealth. But in 2026, with
                the complexity of modern portfolios (multiple brokers, SIPs, SGBs, global stocks), <strong>manual
                    tracking has become a liability</strong>.</p>

            <p>If you are spending more time <em>updating</em> your spreadsheet than <em>analysing</em> your wealth,
                this article is for you.</p>

            <div
                style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2rem; background: var(--bg-surface); border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">1. No Real-Time Pricing (The Lag Effect)</h2>
                <p><strong>The Sheet Reality:</strong> You rely on <code>GOOGLEFINANCE()</code> functions that break
                    half the time, or worse, you manually update prices every weekend.</p>
                <p><strong>The Problem:</strong> Markets move fast. If you are making decisions based on Friday's
                    closing price on a Tuesday morning, you are flying blind. A dedicated tracker keeps your portfolio
                    value live, syncing with NSE/BSE automatically.</p>
            </div>

            <h2>2. The Corporate Action Nightmare</h2>
            <p>What happens to your Excel sheet when:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Reliance announces a 1:1 bonus?</li>
                <li>HDFC twins merge?</li>
                <li>ITC demerges its hotel business?</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>You have to manually adjust historical buy prices.</strong> If you forget, your XIRR calculation
                is ruined forever. Dedicated trackers handle splits, bonuses, and mergers automatically at the backend,
                preserving the integrity of your performance data.</p>

            <h2>3. The "XIRR" Formula Trap</h2>
            <p>Excel has an <code>=XIRR()</code> formula, but using it correctly for a running SIP portfolio requires
                maintaining a perfect chronological list of <em>every single cash inflow and outflow</em>.</p>

            <p>Missed one dividend payout entry? <strong>Wrong XIRR.</strong><br>
                Entered a sell transaction as a positive instead of negative? <strong>Wrong XIRR.</strong></p>

            <p>Arthavi's engine parses your <strong>CAS (Consolidated Account Statement)</strong> to reconstruct your
                transaction history with forensic accuracy, guaranteeing a true performance picture.</p>

            <h2>4. The "Pinch and Zoom" Mobile Experience</h2>
            <p>Trying to view a 30-column wide spreadsheet on an iPhone is a miserable experience. You pinch, you zoom,
                you scroll, and you accidentally type "fgbh4" into a formula cell.</p>
            <p>We built Arthavi to be <strong>mobile-first</strong>. Your wealth dashboard should look as beautiful on
                your phone as it does on your desktop.</p>

            <h2>5. The Privacy Paradox</h2>
            <p>Many investors stick to Excel because they (rightly) don't trust apps that ask for email access.
                <strong>"I don't want an app reading my bank OTPs,"</strong> is a valid concern.</p>

            <p>But local Excel files are risky too:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Hard drive crashes = Data gone.</li>
                <li>File corruption = History lost.</li>
                <li>Version control (<code>Portfolio_Final_v3_REAL.xlsx</code>) = Confusion.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="glass-panel" style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--primary-glow);">
                <h2 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--primary-glow);">The Solution: Excel's Privacy + App's Power</h2>
                <p>We built <strong><a href="/index" style="color: var(--text-head);">Arthavi</a></strong> to
                    give you the best of both worlds.</p>

                <ul style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    <li><strong>Privacy of Excel:</strong> We DON'T ask for your email password or read your SMS. You
                        upload your CAS file manually.</li>
                    <li><strong>Power of an App:</strong> Real-time prices, automated XIRR, corporate action handling,
                        and beautiful mobile UI.</li>
                    <li><strong>AI Insights:</strong> Can your spreadsheet tell you if you are over-exposed to mid-cap
                        stocks? Our "Ask AI" feature can.</li>
                </ul>

                <div style="margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center;">
                    <a href="https://app.arthavi.com" class="btn btn-primary">Upgrade from Excel for Free</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h2>Conclusion</h2>
            <p>Excel was a great tool for the 2010s. But in the 2020s, with multiple asset classes and volatile markets,
                you need a smarter co-pilot.</p>
            <p>Don't be a data entry clerk for your own wealth. Be a portfolio manager.</p>

        </article>
    </main>

